  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Humid with additional showers/thunderstorms \npossible into late week. \n\nA weak cold front over far northern PA late this afternoon\nresulted in the formation of isolated showers and storms. The \nconvection also was near the northern edge of the CI deck, which\nresulted in better heating. Also there was some low level\nconvergence noted in the wind field just south of the front, in\nspots like IPT.\n\nAnyway, the convection is largely over with across the north.\n\nLooking to further to the west to Ohio and points west, not\nseeing much going on, even with rather high dewpoints across\nthe central Great Lakes area. SPC has trimmed the outlook back\nto the west for the overnight hours. \n\nA lot of clouds across the north as of late evening, but still\nexpect patchy fog by early Wednesday morning.\n\nMore information below.\n\nUncertainty only grows with time through midweek. Slow moving\nfrontal boundary will continue risk of showers and heavy\nthunderstorms through Thursday; however tomorrow (8/12) appears\nto mark a nadir in both severe storm and flash flood risk. \n\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Seasonably cooler and less humid Friday and\nSaturday \n\nComfortably cooler and noticeably drier (less humid) air \naccompanies seasonably strong/Canadian high pressure building \nsoutheast from the Upper Midwest Friday night through Saturday.  \nBelow normal pwats will facilitate pleasant days and crisp\nnights (40s and 50s most locations Friday night/AM Saturday).",
